Negative control for the tri-state CLEAR path (P1-R7).

Drops the unset guard from `write`, so a cleared leaf is ASSIGNED empty instead
of being removed from the column — the filter keeps an `eq` key on the wire
after being asked to clear. Any assertion that reads the WIRE (the cleared `eq`
leaf is absent) goes red; one that only reads the control's own pressed state
stays green, because `selected` maps a nil leaf back to the unset value — which
is the point.

Supersedes an earlier version that dropped the guard from `onPick` instead.
That mutation was inert: `FILTER_UNSET_VALUE` is `""`, and lodash `find` with
`{ value: undefined }` or `{ value: "" }` matches no option, so the clear still
resolved to `undefined` and still landed. The guard `write` owns is the one that
carries the behaviour.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

diff --git a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
--- a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
+++ b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
@@ -368,10 +368,7 @@ function leaf(operator: RequestFilterOperator): unknown {
  * `""` mean unset: the leaf is removed rather than written empty.
  */
 function write(operator: RequestFilterOperator, value: unknown): void {
-  const column =
-    isNil(value) || value === ""
-      ? omit(control.value.data, operator)
-      : assign({}, control.value.data, { [operator]: value });
+  const column = assign({}, control.value.data, { [operator]: value });
 
   handleChange(control.value.path, column);
 }
